                    "line": 133,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Jagpal S Gill",
                        "email": "paligill@gmail.com",
                        "username": "jagpalgill"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't see you are doing any exception handling in the caller https://github.com/openbmc/phosphor-bmc-code-mgmt/blob/e793150ace1a40145fa12dc1718ccac14d086a49/common/src/device.cpp#L167. So, lets change the API signature instead to return std::optional<SoftwareVersion::VersionPurpose> and return std::nullopt in case of error and do the due handling in the caller."
                },
                {
                    "file": "common/src/software.cpp",
                    "line": 133,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Alexander",
                        "email": "alexander.hansen@9elements.com",
                        "username": "pointbazaar"
                    },
                    "message": "Sure. This would have been my preference as well but i was not sure you would be ok with changing the api like that."
                }
            ],
